; 01-input-read-whole.l0 -- a program that never looks at its input.
;
; Blocks: linefilter, counter (memory proportional to one line or to the
; state, rather than to the input).
;
; Section 9 has the host read standard input to end of file and build the
; whole (list int) before main is called. So even a program that ignores its
; input pays for all of it, at 16 bytes per input byte (one cons cell), plus
; the read buffer. No allocator change fixes this: the list is live as a
; whole when main is entered, because main's parameter refers to its first
; cell. See measure.sh for the numbers.

(def main ((input (list int))) int
  0)
